{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Include","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is dropped.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Unknown keys go to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"debug!","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so an alias kept in an included file (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"config.d/*","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", the line OrbStack and Colima add) is dialed raw. Fix: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ConfigReader::include","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" splices the files in place — relative paths under the ssh directory, globs expanded in sorted order, missing files skipped, at most 16 levels deep as in OpenSSH — skips an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Include","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" inside a block that does not apply, and writes the including block's header again when an included file opened a block of its own. It only reads.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":{"ordered":5}},
